What:		/dev/esp32p4-parlio
Description:
		One blocking read or write transfers one parallel I/O frame
		using the board's configured data width. Reads sample the
		external RX clock. Writes generate the TX clock.

		ESP32P4_PARLIO_IOC_FRAME in linux/esp32p4-parlio.h transfers
		one frame in one or both directions. It arms RX before
		starting TX when both buffer addresses are supplied. Both
		buffers are length bytes. Pass zero as the address of an
		unused direction, or as the width to use the board default.
		Supported widths are powers of two from 1 through the
		number of wired data lanes.

		The limit is 4096 bytes per frame. A 16-bit frame must
		have an even byte count. TX uses the highest data pin for
		internal clock gating at widths below 16 bits. At 16 bits
		all lanes carry data and the receiver uses the frame length
		to delimit reception.

		The driver sends the most significant sample group of each
		byte first on buses narrower than eight bits. Within a
		group, the bit number matches the data lane number. On
		16-bit buses the low eight lanes carry the low byte.

		Reads and paired transfers time out if the expected number
		of samples does not arrive. The deadline uses the board's
		expected clock rate, frame length and interrupt margin.
		Nonblocking operations return EAGAIN.
